# Web app (Next.js)

## Components

- **Functional only.** No class components.
- File name = component name in `PascalCase.tsx`.
- One component per file unless a tightly-coupled sub-component is private to the parent.
- Default export only for Next.js route files (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`).

## State

| Concern | Tool |
|---|---|
| Server data + cache | TanStack Query |
| Live WebSocket state | Zustand store in `apps/web/lib/store/` |
| Form state | React Hook Form |
| Theme / locale | next-intl + Tolgee |

Never duplicate server state into Zustand — the cache is the source of truth for fetched data.

## Auth token storage

```typescript
// ❌ persistent
localStorage.setItem('accessToken', token);
sessionStorage.setItem('accessToken', token);

// ✅ in memory only
const accessToken = useAuthStore((s) => s.accessToken);
```

On 401: silent refresh via `POST /auth/refresh` (cookie-based). On failure: redirect to `/login`.

## Design tokens

Use Tailwind classes mapped to design-system tokens. **Never hardcode hex.**

```tsx
// ❌
<div style={{ color: '#F59E0B' }} />

// ✅
<div className="text-amber-500" />   // or whatever the token resolves to
```

Branch colours are mixed with surface, never full-saturation as a fill except on map markers (see `design-system §2.1`).

## Error boundary

A global `ErrorBoundary` lives in `app/layout.tsx`. Wrap individual feature panels in their own boundary if they can fail independently (map, dispatch panel).

## Performance

- `useMemo` / `useCallback` only when profiling shows it matters.
- MapLibre vehicle markers interpolate client-side from `Dispatch.routeGeometry` + `dispatchedAt` — no server polling.
- Use `<Suspense>` with skeletons for lazy panels.

## Forbidden

- Hardcoded English UI strings — every string goes through `useT` (see `i18n.mdc`).
- Inline `<script>` (CSP forbids it).
- Direct DOM manipulation (`document.querySelector`); use refs + state.
- Importing from `apps/backend` or `apps/worker`.
